      "side": 1,
      "message": "Android13.5-10 had around ~60 S2MPU patches with a lot of history that is not relevant to keep moving forward. So initially the plan(discussed with @willdeacon) was to push two new patches, one with IOMMU layer, that can be used with EL2 modules and one with S2MPU driver.\n\nAfter discussion with @dbrazdil, to make it easier to review, we agreed to separate the patches to Android13.5-10 port and new features (Modules and new S2MPU version)\nAnd we can just diff the Android13.5-10  patches against Android13.5-10 code,\nand do proper review for the new code.",
